  "text": "### Review Summary (`needs_changes`)\n\n#### Findings\n- **[blocker] `packages/excalidraw/tests/selection.test.tsx:1465`** \u2014 In `describe(\"lasso selection mode\")`, `setup()` renders `<Excalidraw />` without setting non-zero viewport dimensions (`h.state.width` and `h.state.height`). Because `restoreOriginalGetBoundingClientRect()` in an earlier suite (`:1142`) leaves jsdom's `getBoundingClientRect()` returning `width: 0, height: 0`, `Renderer.getVisibleCanvasElements` (`isElementInViewport`) culls every element whose bounding box does not contain `(0, 0)` from `h.app.visibleElements` (`rect2` at `x: 100` in the group test and `child` at `x: 50, y: 20` in the frame tests), so `LassoTrail.updateSelection()` never evaluates them.\n  - **Fix:** Set `h.state.width = 1000` and `h.state.height = 1000` inside `act(() => { ... })` in `setup()` (matching `packages/excalidraw/tests/lasso.test.tsx:47-48`) so all scene elements in the suite are included in `h.app.visibleElements`.\n\n#### Passing Checks\n- **Correctness (`lasso/utils.ts`, `lasso/index.ts`, `CHANGELOG.md`):** Implements `boxSelectionMode` (`\"contain\"` default vs `\"overlap\"`), full-outline and bound-text containment, Liang-Barsky frame-child clipping, and top-level group containment per `change_plan.md`.\n- **Type safety:** Strict TypeScript types throughout (`BoxSelectionMode`, `Bounds`, `GlobalPoint`, `LineSegment<GlobalPoint>`); `yarn test:typecheck` passes with no `any`.\n- **Lint & formatting:** `yarn test:code` and `prettier --check` pass on all 5 touched files.\n- **Unit tests (`packages/excalidraw/tests/lasso.test.tsx`):** All tests pass, including the new Wrap vs Overlap suite.",
